+turns the pathwise increment moduli and deterministic variation bound into
+\(\int M_t^2\,dP=0\).  The full locally bounded-variation statement is obtained
+by stopping or localizing at increasing variation levels and then letting the
+level tend to infinity on the event where the localized process agrees with the
+original process up to \(t\).  The deterministic bound on \(M_t\) gives
+integrability of \(M_t^2\).
+\end{proof}
